    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0319" n="5" xml:id="pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.0012/531t</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-14">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Eighteen treaties ratified yesterday. Is Great Britain disposed to sign treaty
                    when approval of Colonies received or does she prefer to wait until the war is
                    over? It would seem desirable to sign as soon as possible in order to cover any
                    dispute that might arise as result of the war. Please report prospect as several
                    other treaties awaiting action of Great Britain and France. Am inquiring of
                    France.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
